# Triumph 1500 front-wheel-drive saloon, 1970-1973.
#
# The Michelotti-bodied 1500 with front-wheel drive, the car that sat below the
# 2000 in the Triumph range. It is NOT a Dolomite (rear-wheel drive, later, with a
# different nose and rear) and NOT a 1500 TC (the later rear-drive car).
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triumph_1500
#
# Dimensions 4.115 x 1.575 x 1.372 m, wheelbase 2.464 m, from the English
# Wikipedia 1500 specifications. Trim takes the modelled width to 1.599 m, 24 mm
# over the published body width, which does not read at pak scale.
#
# Colours are Triumph paint names of the period — Pimento, White, French Blue and
# Emerald — but **no model-specific dated UK colour list for the 1500 FWD was
# established**. They are period-correct Triumph finishes, not proven factory
# offerings for this model, and the header says so. The intro and retire months
# are road-presence dates. Weights pimento 3, white 3, frenchblue 2, emerald 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 140 km/h, the published figure for the 1500. Comfort 70/435, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 70, the same as the BMC1100 and a step below the 2000 Mk1.
# Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: October 1970 intro, retires staggered 1985-1988 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/triumph-1500.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/triumph-1500.dae (68 objects). References:
# citycars/references/triumph-1500/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitation: the pack holds only three photographs and no side profile,
# so the proportions are dimension-calibrated rather than measured from a
# photograph. Accepted deviations: the nose corners and outer lamp surrounds are
# simplified and the lower body is squarer than the car. At 128 px the Michelotti
# cabin, the paired round lamps and the split grille read as the 1500.

obj=citycar
name=Triumph1500(Pimento)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1970
intro_month=10
retire_year=1988
retire_month=6
speed=140
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=435

